1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,220
Around the Prophet's Mosque
stand 112 gates and doors —

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,700
and every visitor wants to find
their way with peace of mind.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:18,830
Prophet's Mosque Visitor Guide: one
map for every gate, door and service.

4
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:27,620
Seventy outer gates and forty-two mosque
doors, colour-coded by their four sides.

5
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:36,150
Type a door's number or name: see its
side, nearest outer gate and street.

6
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:42,020
Many doors carry a story in their
name — the guide tells it in brief.

7
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:51,650
For women: women's section doors,
restrooms and prayer areas — in one tap.

8
00:00:52,450 --> 00:01:00,680
At Gate 37: whose turn it is now at
the Noble Rawdah, and when it changes.

9
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:06,200
From where you stand, it draws a walking
route through the plaza walkways,

10
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:10,940
with distance and time — and
updates what's left as you walk.

11
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,600
Six languages.

12
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:22,390
Right from the browser — no app-store
download, no permissions to run.

13
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:29,670
Prophet's Mosque Visitor Guide — arrive
with ease, and give your visit your heart.
